Thanks for all the thoughts everyone! After seeing Dan's evidence I agree that it was likely a typo in the text. I thought I was missing some deeper meaning in the code. Always thankful for this group.

On Wednesday, July 24, 2019 at 6:30:27 AM UTC-7, Daniel Linden wrote:

> Yeah, I think it's just a typo that should read:
>
> log(lambda[s,t]) <- beta0 + beta1*chap[s] + beta2*(t - T/2)
>
> If you look at the previous code on page 512 of the AHM book, they had beta.trend*(t-2.5) when T was 5.  So it seems clear they were trying to center by the midpoint year, like Emily suggested.
>

